  id: aa5
  title: Progress
  content: 'The main indicators of player progress are accumulated <b>Experience</b>,
    <b>Fame</b>, and <b>Reputation</b>. These parameters directly affect the hero''s
    effectiveness in combat, the ability to buy or craft better equipment, and to
    hire trained fighters or useful support units.


    <b>Experience</b> - By earning
    experience, the hero increases their <b>Level</b>, and with each level increase,
    their stats, and consequently their power, improve, and new equipment and quests
    become available;


    <b>Fame</b> - The higher this indicator, the more people
    will be willing to follow you. By winning battles, you increase your fame, but
    if you lose, you will lose it;


    <b>Reputation</b> - Determines how you will
    be treated in society. Some people will not want to deal with you if you have
    a bad reputation, however, in criminal circles, this will play into your hands.
    Almost every action or quest in one way or another affects the player''s reputation.'
  section: 4
